 "title": "Regulatory Genomics and Bioinformatics Tools",
 "summary": "This cluster is centered around regulatory genomics and bioinformatics tools, specifically focusing on the E. coli K-12 MG1655 organism. The GIDEON method identifies BPMs, which in turn identify and trim the Liany-ILP and LocalCut methods. The CRP regulon regulates several genes, including adenylate cyclase, crr, and cyaA. The E. coli K-12 MG1655 organism has regulatory features and regulons, and is involved in ALE experiments. The cluster also includes various genes, pathways, and operons, as well as bioinformatics tools like ILP and LocalCut.",
